<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25031" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διᾰκούω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ακούσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Act.Ap.</u>
					23.35
				</span></i>
			:—<i>hear out</i> or <i>to the end,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				11.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					<u>Epit.</u>
					471
				</span></i>
			: abs., of a court, <i>try out</i> a case, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				335.71
			</span></i> (Pergam.); <i>hear</i> or <i>learn</i> from another, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὸς ἄττα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					338d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρά τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theopomp.Hist.
					244
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τά δόξαντα τοῖς ἄρχουσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1273a10
				</span></i>
			: c. gen. rei, [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγων</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prm.</u>
				126c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν λεγομένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					6.58.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.15.4
				</span></i>
			: c. gen. pers., of parties to a dispute, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				599.20
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">Priene</span>), <i><span class="en">
				685.29
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Crete</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>PGrenf.</u>
				1.11i8
			</span></i><span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, <u>Act.Ap.</u>l.c., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. μου πρὸς αὐτούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					168.28
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				3.924.16
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; also, <i>to be a hearer</i> or
				<i>disciple of,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.96S.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ γεωμετρικά τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.L.
					8.86
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Herc.</u>
				862.3
			</span></i>.</div>
